  "_about": "SCULPTED (2026-11-05, docs/engines.md 'the sculpt overlay'): a heavy reptile 5.5 m from its middle head's nose to its tail -- a deep scaled trunk with a pale banded belly, a row of spines down the back onto the tail, columnar legs set a little out on broad four-clawed feet; three necks rising from one broad base on the chest (the rig's arcs, as they were), pale-throated and spined, each to a dragon head -- a long snout, brow ridges, swept-back horns (curved tubes, ringed, dark-tipped), the mouth line carved in with its teeth, slit-pupilled amber eyes set in sockets under the brows (2026-11-07: the overlay's `eyes` as a list, one a head and side) SHARP PASS 2 (2026-11-08): the pointed parts -- clawF, clawH, neckAHorn, neckAHorn2, neckAToothL, neckAToothR, neckBHorn, neckBHorn2, neckBToothL, neckBToothR, neckCHorn, neckCHorn2, neckCToothL, neckCToothR (38 in all) -- are the engine's sharp `horn`s (sharp.js), made from the field shapes they replaced by tools/creaturegen/sharp/ (claws.py, teeth.py, spikes.py, antlers.py, bills.py): rooted in the body, tips pointed; RE-RUN those after this species' generator. (2026-11-08, review.py: claws) The claws RE-ROOTED (review.py): each a sheath as wide as the claw where it leaves the toe, sunk in it, the join faired (horn `fair`: grown out of the skin in its paint), darker at the base fading to its own colour at the point -- no pale cut edge where it leaves the fur.",
